<body>
<section>
<p><strong>Chapter One: Morning</strong></p>
<p>Mist settles over the river landing at dawn. Boatmen tie up their boats while children run to school.</p>
<p>An old banyan tree stands west of the village, and everyone rests in its shade at noon.<sup>1</sup></p>
<p>Rice</p>
<p>Jute</p>
<p>Mustard</p>
<p><strong>Crop</strong></p>
<p><strong>Month</strong></p>
<p>Rice</p>
<p>November</p>
<p>Jute</p>
<p>August</p>
<p><image l:href="#img_1"/></p>
</section>
<section>
<p><strong>Chapter Two: Market</strong></p>
<p>The market meets twice a week. People bring vegetables and handicrafts from distant villages.</p>
<p>When a storm threatens in the afternoon, the sellers pack up their goods in a hurry.</p>
</section>
<section>
<p><strong>Chapter Three: Evening</strong></p>
<p>Lamps are lit in the courtyards at dusk, and the elders tell stories of the old days.</p>
<p>Late at night only the crickets and the current of the river can be heard.</p>
<p>Back to chapter one</p>
</section>
<section>
<p>1 People believe the banyan tree is nearly two hundred years old.</p>
</section>
